&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Build automation that powers the heart of our customers’ most critical operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schuberg Philis, we specialize in mission‑critical IT, partnering closely with our customers to keep their most essential systems running smoothly and securely with 100% responsibility. Our impact is driven by engineers who are deeply technical, automate everything, collaborate naturally, stay curious, take full end‑to‑end ownership, and understand the full stack - from application to core infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for engineers who flourish in automation‑first, mission‑critical environments and want to shape the platforms our customers rely on daily. In a self‑steering customer team, you design, build, run, and improve business‑critical systems across the full stack. You automate everything you touch, streamline pipelines, solve issues across the stack, and tune applications for performance. Working in a culture of real ownership, deep collaboration, and zero silos, where teams carry full responsibility for mission‑critical systems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;/&amp;nbsp;What you will do&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mission‑Critical Automation Engineer, you design, build, run, and improve platforms. You automate everything you touch, diagnose and resolve issues across the entire stack, collaborate closely with customer teams, and take full end‑to‑end ownership of stability, security, and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your day-to-day includes:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building automation through scripting and configuration management tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the full Plan–Build–Run lifecycle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solving multi‑layer issues across OS, network, DB, security, and apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and executing controlled releases with Git and pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Platform‑hardening practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;/&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-parastyle=&quot;No Spacing&quot;&gt;What you bring&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong automation mindset, with hands-on experience in advanced scripting and configuration management (e.g. Powershell, Ansible, DSC, Puppet, Chef).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Git and CI/CD practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying security principles in mission-critical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in Infrastructure-as-Code tooling such as Terraform, Bicep, or ARM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An ownership mentality, combined with curiosity and analytical thinking to understand and improve system behaviour end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of networking, database fundamentals, release/deployment lifecycles, and applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The following would be a plus:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building and running containerized environments (Docker).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Orchestrating platforms using Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operating in public or private cloud environments (Azure, AWS, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;/ Who are you?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An engineer with strong specialization in a core technical domain, combined with a solid understanding of the broader system landscape.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Automation-driven, preferring code over manual work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A pragmatic problem solver who collaborates openly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter who thrives in a high-trust engineering culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated by complex systems, customer impact, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;/&amp;nbsp;What can you expect?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with highly skilled engineers who focus on automation, security, and delivering real customer impact. We prioritize quality and ownership over billable hours (“freedom &amp;amp; responsibility”).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A culture that supports continuous growth through training, mentoring, and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High-quality offices, strong tech community involvement, and opportunities to experiment with new technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re an engineer in the Netherlands who defaults to automation, enjoys deep technical challenges, and drives real customer impact, we’d like to get in touch!&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion in the tech industry.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;At Catawiki, every day brings the extraordinary! Whether it’s &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/583-sports-memorabilia&quot;&gt;Daniel Ricciardo’s Formula 1 Car&lt;/a&gt;, a &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/579-fossils&quot;&gt;Woolly Mammoth’s Skeleton&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/l/10035805&quot;&gt;Lady Gaga&#39;s Jumpsuit&lt;/a&gt; or &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/en/c/583-sports-memorabilia&quot;&gt;Usain Bolt’s running shoe&lt;/a&gt;, we encounter exceptional objects every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a one-of-a-kind marketplace for buying and selling special objects. Each week, more than 100,000 unique items are auctioned, all carefully curated by our passionate in-house experts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Having sold over 25 million unique objects, our mission is to become the world’s most popular destination for special objects. As a growing, diverse and sustainable scale-up, we proudly live by three core values. If these values resonate with you, we’d love to explore how you can join us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Taking ownership and driving impact&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being open to change and feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Being passionate about our mission and our customers.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Every Product Manager at Catawiki owns a meaningful part of the customer experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Search and Ranking, your mission is to help buyers find the special objects they care about. You will shape how search, ranking and personalisation work across the buyer journey, making discovery more relevant and helping more buyers find objects they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a broad product area. It brings together buyer needs, expert curation, marketplace priorities, search experiences and machine learning. You will identify the most important opportunities, set a clear direction and lead a cross functional team from insight to measurable customer and business impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The solution is not prescribed. You may improve search relevance, ranking, recommendations or personalisation, or explore new AI enabled ways to help buyers discover objects. What matters is that you solve a meaningful customer problem, measure the impact and scale what works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own the strategy, outcomes and execution for this area, working closely with Engineering, Design, Data Science, Marketing and Commercial teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set and communicate a clear product vision, strategy and roadmap for Search and Ranking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own measurable outcomes across search relevance, discovery, engagement and buyer conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use behavioural data, customer research and commercial insight to identify and prioritise the biggest opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn ambiguous customer and business problems into clear hypotheses, prototypes and executable plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead initiatives from early discovery through experimentation, launch and scaling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success metrics and build a rigorous experimentation agenda for search, ranking and personalisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with machine learning engineers and data scientists to assess model quality, test new approaches and improve customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the relevance of search results and recommendations across the buyer journey.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate personalisation into the customer experience in ways that feel useful, coherent and trustworthy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, run and evaluate experiments, using positive, negative and inconclusive results to guide decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI and rapid prototyping to test ideas early, reduce development risk and accelerate learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create clarity, momentum and accountability across teams, including when priorities or incentives differ.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate strategy, performance, tradeoffs and recommendations clearly to senior and C level stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Three qualities matter most in this role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;em&gt;Outcome ownership&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You take responsibility for customer and business results, not only for delivering features. You stay with the problem, remove obstacles and change direction when the evidence calls for it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;em&gt;Systems thinking&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You understand how search, ranking, recommendations, auction dynamics, expert curation and marketplace health influence one another. You make thoughtful decisions across the full buyer journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;em&gt;Experimental rigour&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You use data, research, prototypes and controlled experiments to make decisions. You learn from negative results and can distinguish meaningful progress from activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also bring:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least five years of product management experience, preferably in consumer ecommerce, marketplaces or another digital product at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a broad product area or customer journey, rather than only individual features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining product strategy or roadmaps for search, ranking, recommendations, personalisation or other machine learning products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence working with product metrics, experiments and commercial performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, running and analysing A/B tests, including tests involving machine learning products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to turn uncertain opportunities into clear hypotheses, prototypes and plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A practical understanding of machine learning concepts and how models become useful product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working closely with machine learning engineers and data scientists to develop and improve customer facing features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort using AI tools to prototype quickly and explore customer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to balance immediate commercial opportunities with longer term product and platform investments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication skills and the ability to influence senior leaders without relying on formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The pace, resilience and judgement to maintain a high standard of execution in an ambiguous environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Where you will be&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is based in Amsterdam. We offer a relocation package for people currently living outside the Netherlands.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;text text-align-left &quot;&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why You&#39;ll Love Working with Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Create a visible impact &lt;/strong&gt;by working at scale in a global organisation serving millions of customers across 80+ categories. In our flat structure, every role has a broad scope and directly impacts both our customers and the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learn and grow&lt;/strong&gt; through our Learning &amp;amp; Development initiatives, including clear development plans and mentorship programmes to support your career progression.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A culture of connection defines us&lt;/strong&gt;. We’re a passionate, diverse team of 800+ Catawikians representing 60+ nationalities. We foster an inclusive and queer-friendly environment where everyone is encouraged to bring their full self to work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Celebrate life’s moments with us. &lt;/strong&gt;You’ll receive a €100 Catavoucher when you join, a €50 Catavoucher on your birthday, and an extra day off each year to “Pursue Your Passion&lt;strong&gt;”&lt;/strong&gt;. We also offer additional leave for key work anniversaries and important life events. Benefits may vary by location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Offices and Way of Working&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Our vibrant offices in Amsterdam and Lisbon are designed to inspire collaboration. Most Catawikians operate in a hybrid setup, combining office-based and remote work, with a minimum of two days per week in the office, unless a role is explicitly stated as fully remote or fully office-based.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interested?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;Apply with an English CV and Cover Letter. By applying, you agree to &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.catawiki.com/conditions/applicant-privacy-policy.pdf&quot;&gt;Catawiki’s Applicant Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; If you’re excited about this role but don’t meet every requirement, we still encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;We may use artificial intelligence (AI) tools to support the review of your application. AI may help us assess how your experience matches the requirements of the role, but hiring decisions are always made by our recruitment team&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>
